    "title": "Wellness Wednesday: Shopping tips for patients with diabetes, prediabetes - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Viecelli ,\n6 hours ago\nLANSING, Mich. (WLNS) – The grocery store can be an overwhelming place when you’re trying to watch what you eat, especially for people with medical conditions like diabetes or prediabetes.\nA new program in New Jersey is teaming up dietitians with patients to help them make healthier choices.\n“Managing diabetes requires so many different aspects – food, medication, wellness – but I’m focusing on food,” Lynette Hem-Lee, a registered dietitian with Inserra Supermarkets, explained. “What they can eat to manage their blood sugar.”\nFor example, Hem-Lee tells patients that very ripe bananas tend to be higher in sugar and whole grain bread gives you more fiber and protein than white.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WLNS 6 News.",
